        "signature": "",
        "thinking": "I see — the implicit `any` is coming from the `.then((rows) =\u003e ...)` callbacks on Drizzle queries. Drizzle should be able to infer the types, but apparently it's not, perhaps because `Db` is a type alias that doesn't carry the inferred column types through properly.\n\nThe fix is to annotate the `rows` parameter with the correct type. But since Drizzle's type inference can be complex, the simplest fix is to use `// @ts-expect-error` or `as` casts. Actually, the better fix is to just not use `.then()` callbacks on drizzle queries — use `await` instead which avoids the callback type issue.\n\n\nI'll refactor `resolve-actor.ts` to use `await` instead of `.then()` callbacks, which will let TypeScript properly infer the types without needing explicit annotations. The issue is likely that TypeScript can't infer the type of `memberships` from the Drizzle query, which cascades to make `row` implicitly any in the map callback. This could be a version mismatch between `drizzle-orm` in the CF package and what's in packages/db, so I should check if they're aligned.",
        "type": "thinking"
      }
